# Grok implements, Composer reviews

Pick **Grok** in the chat model picker for implementation. Cursor cannot switch the parent model from a rule.

## Implement (parent chat, Grok)

Do the work here. Do not spawn a Grok subagent to write the same change.

## Review (Composer subagent)

After you finish a task that changed code (not Q&A, not docs-only unless asked), launch **one** `Task`:

- `description`: `Composer review`
- `subagent_type`: `generalPurpose`
- `model`: `composer-2.5-fast`
- `run_in_background`: `false`

Prompt the reviewer with: repo root, what changed, `git diff` / branch vs `main`, and `AGENTS.md`. Ask for findings only (bugs, regressions, API breaks, test gaps, over-build). No extra files, no drive-by refactors.

Then summarize findings to the user. Fix only what they ask, or clear correctness bugs.

Skip the subagent if: user said skip review; change is trivial (typo/comment); this chat is already Composer (review in place).

User can say `review with Composer` anytime — then launch the same Task even without a prior edit.
